## The two ratings

- **COMPLEXITY** — how much human-AI interaction is still needed to nail down
  the specifics. `low`: an implementer can proceed from the plan without asking
  anything. `medium`: a few details will need confirming along the way. `high`:
  expect real back-and-forth before the work settles.
- **RISK** — the blast radius if the work is wrong. `low`: contained, easy to
  notice and revert. `medium`: touches shared behavior or data others rely on.
  `high`: could corrupt durable state, break many users, or be hard to undo.

They are independent: a one-line change can still be high risk, and a long plan
can still be low risk.

